  "description": "Reid eTrail 2 250W | Electric mountain bike\nMid-drive power. Trail-ready performance.\nThe Reid eTrail 2 250W is an electric mountain bike designed for challenging trails and off-road riding. Its alloy frame features internal cable routing and an integrated 418Wh battery for a clean finish and balanced handling. Updated geometry, including a longer reach, lower stand and slacker head angle, provides a riding position suited to more demanding terrain.\nThe Ananda 250W 36V mid-drive motor delivers 80Nm of torque, providing responsive assistance and helping riders tackle steep climbs and varied trails. The integrated 36V 11.6Ah battery powers the system, while the Ananda D18 Bluetooth display provides clear ride data and smartphone app compatibility.\nAn SR Suntour suspension fork with 120mm of travel helps absorb impacts from roots, ruts and rocky sections. The Shimano 9-speed drivetrain combines Shimano shifters with a Shadow rear derailleur, an Ananda 170mm 34T narrow-wide chainset and an 11–46T Shimano Cues cassette for a wide gear range across changing gradients.\nTektro hydraulic disc brakes with 180mm rotors provide consistent braking performance on varied terrain. The 29-inch wheels are fitted with 29 x 2.25-inch tyres for traction, stability and rollover capability, while 740mm alloy riser handlebars supports confident handling. An MTB saddle and ergonomic rubber grips complete the setup.\nThe Reid eTrail 2 250W is ideal for:\n\nChallenging trails – Updated geometry designed for more demanding off-road riding\n\nSteep climbs – Ananda mid-drive motor delivering 80Nm of torque\n\nTechnical terrain – SR Suntour fork with 120mm of suspension travel\n\nVersatile gearing – Shimano 9-speed drivetrain with an 11–46T cassette\n\nControlled braking – Tektro hydraulic disc brakes with 180mm rotors\n\nTrail traction – 29-inch wheels with wide 2.25-inch tyres\n\nResponsive handling – 740mm riser handlebars\n\nConnected riding – Ananda D18 Bluetooth display with app compatibility\n\nPlease make sure to familiarise yourself with eBike safety information before charging or using your new Reid. You can view and download user manuals and safety instructions here.",
